  "worked_solution": "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x+1):$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14189988/assets/4d81187377609f2cc79f2f972b1416a00f854d8c7a72731eb306aaa17d9f7339.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x+1)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Moreover, from the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x+1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x+1))=\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))=2.\n$$",
